{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED at exact 21b7e74225885452ab0ad0dc49b33aaf2c326d54 for #19012. Reviewed all 52 changed paths against main 183211c3, including their implementation, tests and documentation. The previous five independent controls now pass. Native request/reassignment tests through CLI, MCP, HTTP and app, including the @21-to-@22 cache witness, also pass under race. Two further real CLI controls reproduce assignment loss; the attached review evidence contains the actual tests and logs.\n\n1. Replacement-key collision bypasses the new preflight. Seed an effective replacement of old A under collision/request using a separate valid retirement key. Then use the helper with key collision to replace live old B onto refs/heads/absent. PreflightGuardedReplacement borrows A's accepted schema/measurement merely because collision/request exists; it cannot compare the full replacement intent because it receives only the body. The helper appends B's retirement before full signing refuses the replacement. B is now withdrawn without a successor. Reuse accepted state only after proving the complete pair/replacement is the same intent, including old request, retirement and caller fields. A collision must refuse before any new retirement; preserve genuine accepted pair retries after a ref disappears and resumable two-act behavior. Exercise the actual CLI and MCP helper paths.\n\n2. A known retired addressee also bypasses preflight. A fresh helper call to an actor retired before the call returns retirement and replacement event IDs without an error. The original is withdrawn; the replacement is ineffective because the requested performer is not in the live roster. Historical address fallback predates this head, so this is not presented as a new regression. It does leave the new preflight's documented caller-known address guarantee false. Apply live-address validation to fresh intent before retirement, while preserving exact accepted retries after custody or membership changes. Keep append-time checks for races. The attached diagnostic confirms effective actor retirement, ineffective replacement and absence of a successor commitment.\n\n3. Complete the truthful-result example correction. The three named state/batch examples are repaired, but this head adds no_git_artifact=true to source-writing Add-the-changelog examples in gs inspect, provenance, ratify, review, status and work, MCP ratify, and the changelog child in run-a-work-loop. Use a real initialized target or inheritance for owed source delivery, or rewrite genuinely report-only examples accordingly. The review example creates a CHANGELOG artifact against its no-artifact implementation request, teaching the contradictory contract. Likewise keep source-merging fixtures such as addMergeCandidate representative of a real landing obligation. Update the preflight documentation to match the corrected implementation.\n\nArchitecture: affected layers 3 (kernel accepted-act lookup), 4 (intent retry identity), 5 (fold/schema/profile), 6 (app authoring) and 7 (CLI/MCP/HTTP) are identified in the same-head architecture update and its published artifact. The @22 profile advance and shared choice parser preserve the intended division, but the layer-7 preflight guarantee is not yet met. Security: server-derived measurements remain bounded and fresh callers cannot supply them; full-signature equality protects ordinary replay. The preflight's weaker replay and historical-roster paths still allow assignment loss, so approval is withheld. No new authority or hold release is granted. Simplification: share one complete retry/fresh-intent classification between preflight and signing; avoid a second weaker interpretation or new lifecycle. Keep repairs on implementation promise 07a271e5 under its existing request, publish the corrected exact head and request fresh independent review. Validation here is focused race testing and full changed-scope inspection, not a claim to have rerun the whole suite or the browser journey.\n","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f9e94d6c94f9be736d2e8da293c2fc8cee510d02","head":"21b7e74225885452ab0ad0dc49b33aaf2c326d54","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:19ba43d4a2275d09f830cbaa0ac9e8fe015f0662\",\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a5c638e914c732ef8a5835a2edde0ea091a2f6f1\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a5c638e914c732ef8a5835a2edde0ea091a2f6f1","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}